            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nI think having `config.content.format` being universally applied to all instances of showing notifications (whether in floating window or in `show_history()`) is a more straightforward design.\r\n\r\nThere are already several approaches to customize this behavior:\r\n- Write custom wrapper that temporarily sets `config.content.format` to what you'd like to see being used when showing history. Here is an example of showing raw message:\r\n    ```lua\r\n    _G.my_show_notifications = function()\r\n      local cur_format = MiniNotify.config.content.format\r\n      MiniNotify.config.content.format = function(notif) return notif.msg end\r\n      MiniNotify.show_history()\r\n      MiniNotify.config.content.format = cur_format\r\n    end\r\n    ```\r\n- Use [`get_all()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/919b953f044d97a2243cc2d1f0b316a199434127/doc/mini-notify.txt#L342) to get all notifications and process them as you'd like (would require creating/showing a special buffer).\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
            "created_at": "2024-10-28T15:22:11Z",
